            "review_title": "Review at Saigon Indian Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Cheryl N\nJohannesburg South, South Africa5 contributions\n0\nSaigon Indian restaurant, great food, lousy service\nAug 2026 • Friends\nWe used Google to find a suitable Indian restaurant that served 2 dishes that we had wanted to have for dinner. \nWe order the below to share, plain dosa, also paratha, sweet passion and a Indian tea to start with.... \nFor main we had the mutton Britain. \nAs per memu, the dosa is served with a sambar and 2 chutneys, we received only one and had to ask, we then received the chutney 20 min into the meal. \nBritain arrived, as per menu this is served with a boiled egg, which it never came with and we had to enquire and the egg arrived just before we could finish up our meal. \nI ordered a 2nd sweet passion when mains arrived and it never came so I share my partners coke. \nThe aloo paratha arrived ahen we were done with the meal, so we took it away. \nBill arrived and I was charged for the 2nd lassi that I never got.... Which I had to ask to be removed. \nThe food is absolutely delicious and so so so good and authentic, however the service is what will not take me back there.\nRead more\nWritten August 17, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
