            "review_text": "Paco F\nHamburg, Germany7 contributions\n0\nEinfach traurig\nNov 2025 • Couples\nHands off – this was by far the saddest restaurant visit we’ve had in Vietnam.\nWe went there as a couple and ordered our food. The service was friendly, but unfortunately only one out of four people spoke English — the others just smiled and nodded without actually understanding. By the time I had almost finished my drink, my wife finally got hers. She asked for non-spicy food, yet her dish was even spicier than mine, which was supposed to be chicken with chili. My portion was quite small.\n\nBe careful: everything is served without rice. When I asked about it, I was simply told that we hadn’t ordered any. I know it differently from Indian restaurants… My starter then arrived when I was already almost done with my main course. Nobody seemed to care about that either.\nThe price-performance ratio at Saigon Indian is terrible.\n\nDo yourself a favor and go to the street food market instead.\nRead more\nWritten November 12, 2025",
