            "review_text": "travelonrepeat_please\nPune, India92 contributions\n0\nEnjoyed South Indian Food\nDec 2023 • Couples\nWe had visited this place for Dinner and this was our second day in Ho Chi Min City. We had ordered Gobi Manchurian, Masala Papad, Masala Dosa, Mysore Masala Dosa and Buttermilk. Dosa's were really nice and Chutneys were tasty. Masala Papad was quite spicy and Manchurian was good. Buttermilk wasn't cold enough else it would have tasted better. While leaving we met the owner of the restaurant and he told us that they are settled in Ho Chi Min city for 20+ years now and also gave us some insights on the temples in the city. I feel it's a good place if you want to eat some South Indian dishes. It is centrally located and very near to Ben Than Market.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten January 3, 2024",
